    {
      "id": "claim_5c33ffad3bf04590b3315e0969c64a93",
      "statement": "Columns are read by headers.indexOf('ColumnName') against the header row, so a typo, extra space, trailing space, or wrong wording returns -1 and silently breaks that field (treated as blank/no-value rather than throwing). Column ORDER does not matter. appendRowToSheet maps object keys to header indices on write, making writes order-independent too.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Profile.gs#L14-L22",
