    {
      "id": "claim_5cc370be75774bc6a957293295f286c1",
      "statement": "patchAuditEventData(txId, eventType, extraFields) re-finds an existing audit row by Transaction_ID + Event_Type (scanning bottom-up), JSON.parses its Event_Data, merges the extra fields in, and writes the stringified result back. It is wrapped in try/catch and never throws because it runs after the action already succeeded; a failed patch must not surface as an action failure. It is how post-commit outcomes (emailSent, emailError, letterFileId, letterError, signedAt) are stamped onto the audit row.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Code/Action.gs#L148-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:584974a52ef6f348658aa2dd997ec72d5df7adcc1b6dd24b3e5ab6cd3150cbfb:"
